WEBVTT

00:01.340 --> 00:04.590
<i>I was about to tell Don Wei
that I was really his daughter,</i>

00:04.760 --> 00:06.470
<i>when he made the mistake
of telling me</i>

00:06.670 --> 00:09.760
<i>he had a daughter back on Earth
that he hadn't seen for a while.</i>

00:10.340 --> 00:12.510
<i>Yeah, right.
Try like 10 years.</i>

00:13.180 --> 00:16.350
<i>I'm afraid only the Ultimate Prize
can bring us together.</i>

00:17.060 --> 00:19.480
<i>If I win, I'll bring
my mother back.</i>

00:19.650 --> 00:21.860
<i>And then we can all live
like a family again.</i>

00:22.610 --> 00:25.530
<i>We've already won our ticket
to Oban for the Grand Finals.</i>

00:25.690 --> 00:27.110
<i>And that's not a bad start.</i>

00:27.740 --> 00:30.860
<i>See you soon, Rick.
And thanks for all your help.</i>

02:32.280 --> 02:34.070
Jordan, wake up.

02:34.610 --> 02:36.030
We've arrived.

02:39.950 --> 02:40.700
Jordan?

02:46.040 --> 02:48.040
You could sleep
through anything.

02:51.960 --> 02:53.880
How did we get down here?

03:10.110 --> 03:11.150
Oban?

03:14.070 --> 03:16.660
Wow.
Look at all these planets.

03:16.950 --> 03:20.200
Hello, Oban.
Prepare yourself to meet Molly.

03:20.450 --> 03:22.580
I'd be careful
if I were you, young lady.

03:22.740 --> 03:24.290
It's a pretty big drop from here.

03:24.710 --> 03:26.120
Huh? What?

03:28.670 --> 03:30.460
But we're miles from the ground.

03:30.630 --> 03:32.250
What kind of place is this?

03:32.420 --> 03:35.050
Until now, everything
we've learned about Oban

03:35.220 --> 03:37.760
is far beyond our comprehension.

03:38.090 --> 03:40.970
Scientists have said for decades
that the center of our Galaxy

03:41.140 --> 03:41.890
was a black hole.

03:42.060 --> 03:44.060
Does this look
like a black hole?

03:44.350 --> 03:46.390
Oban is amazing.

03:51.360 --> 03:54.860
Planet Oban
and the Ultimate Prize.

04:02.120 --> 04:03.950
Where is everyone?

04:05.450 --> 04:07.460
Well, you snooze, you lose.

04:18.470 --> 04:19.510
Hey, there!

04:20.590 --> 04:22.890
Anybody home?

04:24.680 --> 04:27.140
I got a bad feeling
about this place.

04:27.310 --> 04:30.150
Come on, Jordan.
At least pretend to be tough.

04:30.520 --> 04:32.190
Hey. Cut it out!

04:33.860 --> 04:34.780
Hey, what?

04:38.320 --> 04:39.950
Molly! Jordan!
Can you hear me?

04:41.700 --> 04:43.160
It just won't budge.

04:43.450 --> 04:45.370
With the tools we brought,
I'm sure we can open it.

04:45.540 --> 04:46.540
Forget it.

04:50.250 --> 04:53.540
We are not dealing
with natural forces here.

04:54.090 --> 04:56.000
We're going back to the module.

04:57.550 --> 04:58.340
But sir...

04:58.510 --> 05:01.050
Molly and Jordan are
the Avatar's guests.

05:01.300 --> 05:02.840
They've not been locked in.

05:03.010 --> 05:05.390
-We've simply been locked out.
-Huh?

05:07.520 --> 05:10.190
Uh, maybe we should have waited
by the door.

05:11.310 --> 05:12.940
We can always go back.

05:13.100 --> 05:14.400
And now that we're inside,

05:14.560 --> 05:16.190
we need to know
what we're up against.

05:21.360 --> 05:22.530
<i>Wow.</i>

05:32.830 --> 05:35.420
I'm really starting
to like this place.

05:36.960 --> 05:37.630
Hey, wait.

05:40.340 --> 05:42.130
I could stay here forever.

05:43.010 --> 05:45.760
Yeah, as long
as it doesn't get too cozy.

05:54.560 --> 05:56.940
Molly, don't even breathe.

05:57.110 --> 05:59.440
-Run for your life when I say go.
-What do you mean?

06:36.690 --> 06:38.650
-Well, hi there.
-Uh...

06:38.820 --> 06:41.150
We're, uh, the Earth team.

06:41.860 --> 06:42.990
Pleased to meet you.

06:48.370 --> 06:50.240
I'm told he won't bite.

06:53.200 --> 06:54.460
Prince Aikka?
What are you...

06:54.620 --> 06:56.420
As long as you don't provoke him.

06:56.580 --> 06:58.420
He's one of the nine finalists.

07:00.170 --> 07:01.170
Thanks, Prince.

07:01.340 --> 07:03.470
But I clued into that one a while ago.

07:13.810 --> 07:16.480
Prince Aikka, I'm so glad
to see you again.

07:18.560 --> 07:19.520
I see.

07:19.690 --> 07:22.480
You still think
we didn't keep our promise.

07:22.860 --> 07:25.860
On my planet, when you make
a promise, you keep it.

07:28.410 --> 07:30.910
But we're also taught
how to forgive.

07:31.080 --> 07:32.870
I am not mad at you, Molly.

07:33.290 --> 07:34.790
Welcome to Oban.

07:41.880 --> 07:44.760
Yeah, thanks for beating Spirit
back on Alwas.

07:44.920 --> 07:47.180
It was a big help.
Put her there, pal.

07:47.510 --> 07:49.640
I said I wasn't mad at Molly.

07:49.800 --> 07:51.640
You are a different matter.

07:52.140 --> 07:54.470
So tell me, how's your cheek?

07:57.020 --> 07:58.600
Come on, guys. Cut it out.

07:58.770 --> 08:00.810
It's challenging enough
on the race track.

08:01.110 --> 08:03.980
Yes, Molly's right.
The preselections were nothing.

08:06.030 --> 08:08.240
These racers are
the best of the best.

08:08.410 --> 08:10.030
We'll need all of our strength.

08:10.410 --> 08:12.580
Have you ever heard
of these creatures before?

08:13.240 --> 08:14.200
Only two.

08:14.580 --> 08:15.660
That's Sul.

08:15.830 --> 08:19.170
He's a powerful magician
known across the entire Galaxy.

08:19.500 --> 08:22.840
Some say his powers match
those of the Avatar.

08:23.000 --> 08:24.050
But I have my doubts.

08:26.380 --> 08:29.130
That's the notorious General Kross
of the Crog lmperium.

08:29.680 --> 08:30.840
<i>What happened to Torus'?</i>

08:31.010 --> 08:33.760
Apparently,
the good colonel lost his head.

08:34.140 --> 08:35.310
Literally.

08:35.470 --> 08:37.390
It seems his superiors
weren't very pleased

08:37.560 --> 08:38.980
with his defeat
against the Earth team.

08:39.440 --> 08:41.650
But he came in first
in the preselections.

08:41.810 --> 08:43.150
Way ahead of everyone.

08:43.610 --> 08:47.110
To the Crogs,
failure is not an option.

08:49.150 --> 08:51.910
I knew Toros had grown soft.

08:52.200 --> 08:55.370
But to lose
against you pitiful humans...

08:55.660 --> 08:58.040
I understand now
why he gave his head

08:58.200 --> 09:00.670
willingly
to the Crog lmperium.

09:03.210 --> 09:04.710
Well, I guess it wasn't his day.

09:08.420 --> 09:11.300
In the name
of my master, the Avatar,

09:11.470 --> 09:16.010
I welcome all the finalists
of the Great Race on Oban.

09:27.530 --> 09:29.940
Satis, what in the world
are you doing here?

09:30.110 --> 09:34.370
We left you on Sangrar,
265.4 light years away.

09:34.990 --> 09:35.950
Huh? Sangrar?

09:36.120 --> 09:38.910
It's one of the three planets
where the preselections were held.

09:39.080 --> 09:41.120
Alwas, Sangrar, and Darwar.

09:43.630 --> 09:46.420
I've been promoted
to spokesperson.

09:46.800 --> 09:50.630
But how could he be on Sangrar
when he was with us on Alwas?

09:52.180 --> 09:55.180
Your attention, please,
winning pilots.

09:55.350 --> 09:57.310
The first match of the Grand Finals

09:57.470 --> 09:59.640
will begin in just a few minutes.

10:00.140 --> 10:02.310
There will be nine races total.

10:02.480 --> 10:05.360
Nine races where you will all
race against one another

10:05.520 --> 10:06.690
at the same time.

10:06.860 --> 10:08.780
But we must study the courses.

10:10.610 --> 10:11.820
Study the courses?

10:11.990 --> 10:14.610
This is the Grand Finals
we're talking about.

10:14.820 --> 10:18.490
The nine races will each take place
in a different region of Oban.

10:19.490 --> 10:21.580
The course of the race
will be marked

10:21.750 --> 10:25.420
only by stone doors,
which you will have to find

10:25.580 --> 10:26.790
and fly through.

10:26.960 --> 10:28.670
There will be no time for study.

10:29.130 --> 10:30.840
Will the scoring rules stay the same?

10:31.970 --> 10:35.220
Just to make things
a little more interesting,

10:35.390 --> 10:38.640
the first three racers
of each round shall receive points.

10:39.140 --> 10:40.890
Nine points for the winner,

10:41.060 --> 10:45.190
six points for second place,
and then three points for third.

10:45.600 --> 10:49.270
The Ultimate Prize will be awarded
to the pilot totaling

10:49.440 --> 10:52.570
the highest number of points
at the end of the nine races.

10:53.320 --> 10:54.070
Got it?

10:54.900 --> 10:59.370
81 points maximum,
with 112 possibilities of scoring.

10:59.530 --> 11:02.910
It's a fair race,
but I will still dominate it.

11:03.450 --> 11:06.250
And remember, any attempt
on a competitor's life

11:06.420 --> 11:07.750
is strictly forbidden.

11:08.210 --> 11:10.880
Who could possibly think
of something like that?

11:11.090 --> 11:14.800
The penalty is
immediate disqualification.

11:16.430 --> 11:17.510
OK, then, everyone.

11:17.680 --> 11:20.220
If you're ready,
we're off to the races.

11:34.820 --> 11:38.160
Stan, Koji, grab on
to whatever you can!

11:43.290 --> 11:45.290
But my ship! My crew!

11:45.710 --> 11:46.960
Not to worry, my friend.

11:47.120 --> 11:49.080
Your housing modules
are coming with us.

12:00.800 --> 12:02.890
Now, hurry.
Go and get ready.

12:03.060 --> 12:04.640
We'll be there soon.

12:08.190 --> 12:10.980
And how are we supposed
to reach our charming modules?

12:11.150 --> 12:13.070
The Avatar expects us to fly there?

12:13.230 --> 12:15.440
He's going to have to give
my partner some wings.

12:16.740 --> 12:18.360
No, that won't be necessary.

12:18.530 --> 12:20.370
Simply use the magical portals.

12:20.700 --> 12:23.530
Ah, the magical portals.
Of course!

12:26.160 --> 12:28.670
Uh, where exactly are
these magical portals?

12:29.040 --> 12:30.290
He's gone!

12:30.540 --> 12:32.420
My ship! My ship!

12:32.710 --> 12:35.050
I guess we'll just have
to find them ourselves.

12:35.300 --> 12:37.670
-Good luck, Prince.
-And to you.

12:38.970 --> 12:40.550
"Good luck, Prince!"

12:41.010 --> 12:43.720
We'll be waiting for you
at the finish line, pal.

12:43.890 --> 12:44.640
Hey!

12:47.890 --> 12:49.640
Shoot, it's closed.

12:49.810 --> 12:51.150
Any ideas?

12:53.860 --> 12:54.980
<i>This way.</i>

13:01.110 --> 13:02.070
Yeah.

13:04.410 --> 13:05.700
Follow me, Molly!

13:11.000 --> 13:12.290
Hey, I'm still here.

13:24.010 --> 13:27.970
I was imagining something
a little more, you know, magical.

13:37.860 --> 13:39.530
Nice of you to drop in.

13:39.740 --> 13:41.070
The race is about to begin.

13:41.400 --> 13:43.450
The Whizzing Arrow 3 is ready.

13:43.610 --> 13:45.370
Stan and Koji are standing by.

13:58.420 --> 14:00.800
What were you doing
with the humans?

14:01.300 --> 14:03.890
A person is judged
by the company they keep.

14:04.390 --> 14:08.010
I wouldn't want you
to fall into the wrong crowd.

14:08.180 --> 14:09.680
I don't know
what you're talking about.

14:09.850 --> 14:11.890
I came here to win, and I shall!

14:12.230 --> 14:14.560
You will not betray us again.

14:16.480 --> 14:20.900
Do not forget the Crogs,
your true friends.

14:38.210 --> 14:40.630
The Whizzing Arrow 3
is ready to roll.

14:45.970 --> 14:46.970
Come on!

14:50.930 --> 14:52.520
Koji, get out of there! Hurry!

15:00.150 --> 15:01.690
Stan! Help me!

15:15.250 --> 15:17.040
We're falling too fast here!

15:21.090 --> 15:22.760
Star-racers aren't meant to fly.

15:23.130 --> 15:24.880
Push all of its reactors to the max.

15:25.340 --> 15:26.220
Got it.

15:48.360 --> 15:50.200
Hull OK at 90%.

15:50.370 --> 15:52.580
Booster drives took
a beating, though.

15:53.160 --> 15:54.540
Excellent work, Molly.

15:54.700 --> 15:57.080
We'll fix this little problem
after the race.

15:57.250 --> 15:58.370
That's a promise.

16:03.800 --> 16:06.840
Satis said stone doors.
Do you see anything on your scanners?

16:07.880 --> 16:10.050
We don't have
enough data yet, Molly.

16:10.220 --> 16:11.890
Keep following the others for now.

16:22.570 --> 16:24.320
Oh, no, no, no, no!

16:28.280 --> 16:31.030
Pull hard on the oars, men!
Broadside the enemy.

16:33.990 --> 16:35.290
Huh? Molly!

16:35.500 --> 16:36.290
Watch out!

16:58.730 --> 16:59.810
Here's the door!

17:03.690 --> 17:04.900
Looks like we've got something.

17:05.070 --> 17:07.150
The stone doors emit
pulsar vibrations.

17:07.320 --> 17:09.570
If I can decode it,
we might be able to trace them.

17:28.170 --> 17:28.970
<i>Hmm...</i>

17:30.680 --> 17:33.140
Jordan, don't be stupid.

17:33.300 --> 17:34.890
I'm just keeping an eye on him.

17:35.050 --> 17:36.640
There's no law
against that, is there?

17:58.410 --> 18:00.870
<i>Unsakai', G'dar shalanar!</i>

18:12.930 --> 18:15.140
Hey, what happened
to "ladies first?"

18:29.570 --> 18:32.570
This Nourasian has yet
to learn his lesson.

18:50.000 --> 18:51.260
What's going on?

18:55.090 --> 18:55.800
Aikka!

19:10.020 --> 19:12.110
Oh, a prince
and his pet beetle.

19:12.360 --> 19:13.990
Is there a prettier sight?

19:21.580 --> 19:24.210
Molly, I absolutely
forbid you to stop.

19:24.370 --> 19:25.580
You have a race to win.

19:34.300 --> 19:37.090
Jordan, have you gone
completely nuts?

19:37.760 --> 19:40.810
You know, Molly, you should have
a little more trust in your partner.

19:41.180 --> 19:43.100
I was just returning a debt.

19:49.770 --> 19:50.940
Thanks, Jordan.

19:51.110 --> 19:52.440
Sorry to doubt you.

19:55.780 --> 19:57.240
Where is everybody?

19:57.700 --> 19:59.620
Koji, where's the next magic gate?

19:59.780 --> 20:01.870
I'm uploading the data
onto your computer.

20:02.030 --> 20:03.120
This might do the trick.

20:09.250 --> 20:10.460
I think it's working.

20:10.630 --> 20:12.880
But we're not even
near the target.

20:19.430 --> 20:20.260
Here it is.

20:53.670 --> 20:54.800
It's over, Molly.

20:54.960 --> 20:58.380
_ Sul came in first place,
O second, and Kross third.

20:58.670 --> 21:00.510
Over? But I...

21:00.680 --> 21:04.350
We came in fifth place,
just behind Ning and Skun.

21:04.510 --> 21:05.510
We have no points.

21:07.060 --> 21:09.520
Head back
to the Flying Temple at once.

21:10.060 --> 21:13.900
I suppose it could have been
a lot worse for our first race on Oban.

21:14.270 --> 21:16.530
No points is like no race at all.

21:16.690 --> 21:18.110
I have to do better.

21:19.280 --> 21:20.570
I don't have a choice.

21:20.740 --> 21:22.360
I have to win the Ultimate Prize.
